    'summary': 'The code executes, but the Fourier cross-validation leaks 
information across contiguous phase blocks: its three-harmonic model is 
evaluated by training on all other blocks and extrapolating into each held-out 
interval, so exceptionally high scores do not establish a robust phase-locked 
trajectory. More importantly, the mean-phase scan includes both phase endpoints 
(0 and 2π) as separate observations; modeling them as ordinary points is 
acceptable descriptively but endpoint agreement/closure is never reported 
despite being central to the proposed question. Fix by using the prespecified 
blocked comparison cautiously (or a valid periodic validation design), and 
explicitly quantify endpoint-direction difference; note that row order as 
acquisition order is unknown.'
